  "Question": "Each edge of a cube is increased by \\(50\\%.\\) The percent of increase of the surface area of the cube is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(50\\)",
    "B": "\\(125\\)",
    "C": "\\(150\\)",
    "D": "\\(300\\)",
    "E": "\\(750\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "A cube has six square faces, so an edge of length \\(s>0\\) gives surface area \\(6s^2\\). Increasing the edge by \\(50\\%\\) changes its length to \\(1.5s\\), giving new surface area\n\\[\n6(1.5s)^2=2.25(6s^2).\n\\]\nThus the new area is \\(225\\%\\) of the original area. The increase is\n\\[\n225\\%-100\\%=125\\%.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{125\\%}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
